# Discord desktop client — its HTTPS side only. Voice is NOT here and must not be: voice is UDP to
# bare IPs, no hostname, so no rule can match it anyway, and it works fine direct once zapret2's own
# raw packets stop being swallowed (see the daemon migration).
#
# Why the tunnel at all: the client runs two TLS stacks. The main one sends a 1785-byte TLS 1.3
# ClientHello and the strategy's Discord profile carries it. The second sends 164-183 bytes of
# TLS 1.2 with no supported_versions and no ALPN, and the DPI kills that shape on every Discord host
# — measured 2026-09-12 against 19 desync variants, including a control with no desync at all. The
# app blocks on it at startup (spinning logo), so these hosts go through the node instead.
discord.com
discord.gg
discordapp.com
discordapp.net
discordcdn.com
discord.media
